B2: You have one B2. Since you have B suit melds, keeping B2 could help form a B suit pair or chow with B1/B3. But B2 is a simple tile, and many are unseen (4 left). Might be worth keeping for Half Flush potential.\n\nReason: The safest and most logical discard is F3 because it's an honor tile with low pairing potential (only 2 unseen F3 left, but others have discarded some), and it doesn't contribute to any suit-based combinations. Keeping your T suit tiles might allow for future chows if you draw, and keeping the T2 pair gives you a potential pair. B2 should be kept to maintain flexibility with your B suit melds for Half Flush. Thus, discarding F3 is a conservative move to reduce honor tiles while preserving options.\n\nAnswer: Play F3"}
